# AGENTS.md — SDDKit Workflow for AI Agents

> Generated by SDDKit {{ sddkit_version }}.

This repository uses **Spec-Driven Development** (SDD). All AI agents working
in this repository must follow this workflow without exception.

## Mandatory Workflow

```
/spec  →  /plan  →  /tasks  →  /implement  →  /review
```

**Never skip a stage. Never begin implementation before all gates are approved.**

## Stage Rules

### 1. /spec
- Create `specs/<feature>/spec.md` with uniquely-numbered requirements.
- Format: `REQ-001`, `REQ-002`, …
- Every requirement must be testable.

### 2. /plan
- Create `specs/<feature>/plan.md`.
- Every REQ-NNN from the spec must appear in the plan.
- Get human approval: `sddkit approve <feature> spec` → then start plan.

### 3. /tasks
- Create `specs/<feature>/tasks.md`.
- Every REQ-NNN must appear in at least one task AND one test task.
- Get human approval: `sddkit approve <feature> plan` → then start tasks.

### 4. /implement
- **Pre-flight:** Run `sddkit check <feature>` — must exit 0.
- **Pre-flight:** Confirm all three approvals in `specs/<feature>/status.json`.
- If either check fails, STOP and ask the human.
- Only modify files listed in the task descriptions.

### 5. /review
- Run `sddkit check <feature>` and `pytest` — both must pass.
- Apply the validator checklist in `.claude/agents/validator.md`.
- Apply any requested domain pack from `kit/packs/`.

## Enforcement Differences: Claude Code vs Cursor

| Mechanism | Claude Code | Cursor |
|---|---|---|
| Real-time gate block | ✔ PreToolUse hook denies writes | ✘ No equivalent hook |
| CLI check | ✔ `sddkit check` | ✔ `sddkit check` |
| Pre-commit | Optional | Recommended |
| CI | ✔ `sddkit eval` in GitHub Actions | ✔ `sddkit eval` in GitHub Actions |
| Always-apply rules | ✔ CLAUDE.md | ✔ `.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc` |

> **Cursor agents:** The absence of a real-time hook means discipline is
> enforced by these rules, `sddkit check` in pre-commit, and CI. The rules
> state this clearly so no agent is surprised by the difference.

## Requirement Traceability

Every REQ-NNN must appear in:
1. `spec.md` (definition)
2. `plan.md` (how it will be implemented)
3. `tasks.md` (what task implements it)
4. A test file in `tests/` (how it is verified)

`sddkit check <feature>` validates all four. It exits non-zero on any gap.

## Secret Hygiene

Never include API keys, tokens, or passwords in any committed file.
Use environment variables or a secrets manager.

## Commit Message Format

```
feat(<feature>): implement REQ-001 — <description>
test(<feature>): add test coverage for REQ-002
fix(<feature>): correct edge case for REQ-003
```
